; Leg DC -- the host SENDS.  The Victor RECEIVES with --xonxoff.
;
; The same reading as DB, on the other mechanism, and it is the one that
; matters for interoperability rather than for this cable: the far end's
; wiring is not something this port can assume, and XON/XOFF needs three
; wires.
;
;     rxpeak ~256-600   the host stopped.  xoff/xon may also be non-zero,
;                       which is the host's OWN tty flow control arriving.
;     rxpeak ~2,4xx     we sent XOFF and nothing happened.
;
; BYTE-EXACTNESS IS LOAD-BEARING HERE in a way it is not for RTS/CTS,
; because this mechanism is in band.  PX_CAU keeps DC1 and DC3 prefixed
; (ckcmai.c:2699), and setprefix() re-prefixes them unconditionally when
; flow is FLO_XONX (2705), so a raw DC1/DC3 on the wire is always a command
; -- but that is an argument, and cmp is a measurement.  cmp FIRST.
;
; Note the Victor removes intercepted XON/XOFF from the stream and does NOT
; count them in rxbytes, on purpose (they are not in the host's packet log).
; The pktstat reconciliation should therefore still be -11.  Under MAME with
; five intercepted characters it was exactly that (SS16aj leg FH).

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set retry 30
set parity none
set flow xon/xoff
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
log packets s16ajDC.pkt
send rcvdc.dat
statistics
